This project is modelled on the Go standard library. It is a reimplementation
and not a fork. No Go source code is copied into core/.

Test data, test tables and conformance corpora are taken from other projects
where doing so is better than inventing our own. Each carries the licence of the
project it came from, each file has an entry in tests/data/PROVENANCE.md naming
its source and the revision it was taken at, and the full set of third party
licences is collected in LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY.

The projects those corpora come from, and the licence each is used under:

  The Go Programming Language          BSD 3-Clause
  Unicode Character Database           Unicode License
  IANA Time Zone Database              Public Domain
  Web Platform Tests                   BSD 3-Clause
  JSONTestSuite                        MIT
  Project Wycheproof                   Apache-2.0
  PngSuite                             PngSuite terms, see LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY
  Public Suffix List                   MPL-2.0

A build of this library does not depend on any of the above at run time.
OpenSSL is a run time dependency of core.crypto and is used under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.
